            {
                "entry_id": "80666190-98f4-35d4-ba71-fdf760ac3505",
                "word": "Midland",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "04fdc160-f812-4f4d-ab7f-9f4258e17559",
                        "entry_id": "80666190-98f4-35d4-ba71-fdf760ac3505",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Midland"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e1fd12c2-4068-48f1-a283-6b9fc9e53ad3",
                        "entry_id": "80666190-98f4-35d4-ba71-fdf760ac3505",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Midland"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e1337b3-3132-342c-be81-9ec1e4576908",
                        "entry_id": "80666190-98f4-35d4-ba71-fdf760ac3505",
                        "glosses": [
                            "From or pertaining to the English Midlands."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9202b37-bc47-4afc-afef-9522b111a209",
                                "sense_id": "8e1337b3-3132-342c-be81-9ec1e4576908",
                                "text": "In the more Midland counties, there are thirteen ; in Staffordshire (Wolverhampton), one; in Warwick (Birmingham), seven; in Nottingham, three; in Leicester, one; and Northampton, one."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c60b488-7680-4c11-b395-427ba2585ba4",
                                "sense_id": "8e1337b3-3132-342c-be81-9ec1e4576908",
                                "text": "The obvious inference was that Midland culture found its centre in Lichfield, and that the only claim to distinction which the larger town could make was based on commercial grounds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60fb6f61-e05c-4503-8e70-0f06088c3bad",
                                "sense_id": "8e1337b3-3132-342c-be81-9ec1e4576908",
                                "text": "His only visit to London had been that on which been touched by Queen Anne for the King's Evil and throughout his life he preserved a Midland accent in his speech."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e445434d-776b-4222-ad27-3453c37ba081",
                                "sense_id": "8e1337b3-3132-342c-be81-9ec1e4576908",
                                "text": "This stimulated sales and suited the needs of small manufacturers in the Midland city, who could not afford to trade on credit."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "907b51d5-10d3-3f9a-95a8-a4bc630cb2d4",
                        "entry_id": "80666190-98f4-35d4-ba71-fdf760ac3505",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to the dialect of American English spoken in the Midwest known as Midland American English."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
